<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · religion</p><h1 class="enc-title">Catholicism</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Catholic</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Catholicism is the faith and practice of the Roman Catholic Church, headed by the pope in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. It was the official religion of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a> and of most of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a>, and the faith of the majority in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a>. Religious conflict with Protestant powers, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swedish-empire">Swedish Empire</a>, shaped the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-years-war">Thirty Years' War</a>, while in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a> Catholics faced Bismarck's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kulturkampf">Kulturkampf</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/catholicism.jpg" alt="Catholicism" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jebulon · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saint_Peter%27s_Basilica_facade,_Rome,_Italy.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
